Package: sigfig
Title: Numeric Vectors with Known Precision
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    c(person(given = "Mitchell",
             family = "O'Hara-Wild",
             email = "mail@mitchelloharawild.com",
             role = c("aut", "cre"),
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6729-7695")))
Description: A semantic data type for numbers with known precision. Each element
    pairs a double precision value with a signed integer precision, describing
    the number of decimal places (or with negative precision, the powers of ten)
    to which the value is known. Values are displayed exactly as described by 
    their precision, and operations on vectors of differing precision give 
    results with the coarsest known precision (e.g. 3.2 + 4.12 is 7.3). Full 
    values are retained in computation, so rounding error does not accumulate. 
    The precision is stored with run length encoding using ALTREP (Alternative
    Representations for R Objects), allowing the same precision to be repeated 
    many times throughout a vector with minimal memory use.
